+## Automatic Jev check
+
+When the audit has a concrete proposed finding and the smallest relevant code
+slice, resolve `${AGENTIC_HOME:-$HOME/.agentic}/artifacts/jev/PROTOCOL.md`
+and follow that shared automatic Jev protocol.
+Send the finding, cited code, and its stated replacement—not the whole repo. Ask
+a Noul whether the cited code actually has the named `delete`, `stdlib`, `native`,
+`yagni`, or `shrink` property; use one question per overlapping tag. Jev is an
+advisory check of an already proposed finding, never a substitute for repository
+search, code understanding, or the required concrete replacement. If the result
+is unavailable, ambiguous, or conflicts with code evidence, inspect normally and
+retain the ordinary audit result. Do not add Jev probabilities to the one-line
+output; the existing report stays authoritative.
+
